    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51910" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθυπερ-έχω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be much superior</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έχων</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥττων</span>,
			Aristeas <i><span class="en">
				257
			</span></i>: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλόγων ζῴων κ. τῷ ἀρετᾶς ἐπίμοιρος
					ἦμεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Euryph.
				</span></i>
			 ap.<i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.39.27
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i>in</i> or <i>by</i> a thing, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.25.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γένει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Callicrat.
				</span></i>
			 ap.<i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.28.18
			</span></i>: rarely c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξουσίαν
			κ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Theano
				<u>Ep.</u>
				5.4
			</span></i>: c. acc. pers. etdat. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὼς ἄλλως ἀρετᾷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diotog.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				4.7.62
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, Ps.<i><span class="en">
				Philol.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Stob.
				1.20.2
			</span></i>.</div>
